PlanetsPos←{
   ⍝ Table of positions of planets ⍵ for dates ⍺
   ⍝ Result is 3D array: dates × planets × coordinates
   ⍝ Each date contributes the planets in ⍵ followed by the comet;
   ⍝ they are joined as the book's loop joins them, by catenation on the
   ⍝ first axis to an empty table, so a scalar ⍵ stacks the rows instead
    pl←Data.planets[,⍵;]
    rows←{(⍵ PlanetPos pl),[1]⍵ CometPos Data.kohoutek}¨,⍺
    ⊃{⍵,[1]⍺}/⌽(⊂(0,(1+⍴⍵),3)⍴0),rows }
